# Copy to `.env` for local use. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it
# must never contain a real value — only names and explanations.
#
# Which of these belong where:
#
#   Netlify  → Site configuration → Environment variables
#   CI       → repository secrets
#   Local    → your shell

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing. Every dependency resolves from the public npm registry or from this
# workspace, so builds need no credentials at all — not locally, not in CI,
# not on Netlify.

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which ContentAdapter the shell injects at server start: "memory" (default)
# or "supabase". Leave unset until the Supabase adapter exists (Phase 5) —
# setting it to "supabase" now throws deliberately rather than silently
# serving fixtures in production.
# CONTENT_ADAPTER=memory

# ── Phase 5, not yet used ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When the Supabase adapter lands, note the split carefully:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL              safe to expose; identifies the project
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY         safe to expose; RLS is what protects the data
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY SERVER ONLY — bypasses RLS entirely
#
# Vite inlines any variable prefixed `VITE_` into the client bundle, where it
# is readable by anyone. The service role key must never carry that prefix,
# and must never be read outside a server function.
